From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:46:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] s2r: keep a core restarted by Linux off the consoles
 (T8132)

Linux's apple_cpu driver (rryan j416c-sleep, carried on the J604 deep
sleep branch) powers secondaries down through the PMGR and starts them
again. A started core resets at its locked RVBAR and runs m1n1's
_cpu_reset_c -> init_cpu -> smp_secondary_entry before it reaches the
spin table release, and on T8132 that path prints (CODE). By then Linux
owns everything m1n1 printed to: the framebuffer m1n1 drew on, the USB
gadget, the UART. The kernel asks for silence by setting QUIET (bit 0 of
the mailbox flags word) before it restarts a core, but nothing here read
it outside the warm boot path.

Add s2r_quiet(): true on the warm boot path or once the mailbox carries
QUIET (read uncached, as the kernel cleaned it to the PoC), and use it in
the three places a restarted T8132 core would print. Other SoCs and the
first boot (mailbox zeroed by kboot) are unchanged.

Not run on a J604 yet (TO-VERIFY on the J604, abort_before=2).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/chickens.c |  2 +-
 src/s2r.c      | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 src/s2r.h      |  1 +
 src/smp.c      |  3 ++-
 src/startup.c  |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/chickens.c b/src/chickens.c
index ae712fd1..91787fac 100644
--- a/src/chickens.c
+++ b/src/chickens.c
@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@ void init_cpu(void)
     int part = FIELD_GET(MIDR_PART, midr);
     int rev = (FIELD_GET(MIDR_REV_HIGH, midr) << 4) | FIELD_GET(MIDR_REV_LOW, midr);
 
-    bool quiet = ((chip_id == T8142 || chip_id == T8152) && !is_boot_cpu()) || s2r_warm_quiet;
+    bool quiet = ((chip_id == T8142 || chip_id == T8152) && !is_boot_cpu()) || s2r_quiet();
     if (!quiet)
         printf("  CPU part: 0x%x rev: 0x%x\n", part, rev);
 
diff --git a/src/s2r.c b/src/s2r.c
index 0bc43d95..83226ae9 100644
--- a/src/s2r.c
+++ b/src/s2r.c
@@ -70,6 +70,23 @@ bool s2r_warm_pending(void)
     return read64((u64)&s2r_mailbox.magic) == S2R_MAGIC;
 }
 
+/*
+ * True while nothing on this core may print: on the warm boot path, and on
+ * any core reset once the kernel has set QUIET in the mailbox (apple_cpu sets
+ * it before it restarts a core through the PMGR). After kboot, Linux owns the
+ * consoles m1n1 printed to (the framebuffer m1n1 drew on, the USB gadget,
+ * the UART), so a restarted secondary must reach the spin table silently.
+ * Caches may be off: this reads what the kernel cleaned to the PoC.
+ */
+bool s2r_quiet(void)
+{
+    if (s2r_warm_quiet)
+        return true;
+    if (!s2r_supported())
+        return false;
+    return read64((u64)&s2r_mailbox.flags) & S2R_FLAG_QUIET;
+}
+
 void s2r_warm_resume(void)
 {
     u64 base = (u64)&s2r_mailbox;
diff --git a/src/s2r.h b/src/s2r.h
index efbc1895..b60bd2ba 100644
--- a/src/s2r.h
+++ b/src/s2r.h
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@ extern bool s2r_warm_quiet;
 
 bool s2r_supported(void);
 bool s2r_warm_pending(void);
+bool s2r_quiet(void);
 void __attribute__((noreturn)) s2r_warm_resume(void);
 int s2r_publish(void *dt);
 
diff --git a/src/smp.c b/src/smp.c
index 8b539ba5..b5dbf65b 100644
--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "cpu_regs.h"
 #include "memory.h"
 #include "pmgr.h"
+#include "s2r.h"
 #include "soc.h"
 #include "string.h"
 #include "types.h"
@@ -226,7 +227,7 @@ void smp_secondary_entry(void)
     else
         msr(TPIDR_EL1, index);
 
-    if (chip_id != T8142 && chip_id != T8152)
+    if (chip_id != T8142 && chip_id != T8152 && !s2r_quiet())
         printf("  Index: %d (table: %p)\n\n", index, me);
 
     me->mpidr = mpidr;
diff --git a/src/startup.c b/src/startup.c
index 088759a7..89cd7fe7 100644
--- a/src/startup.c
+++ b/src/startup.c
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ void _cpu_reset_c(void *stack)
         smp_secondary_entry();
         return;
     }
-    bool quiet = chip_id == T8142 && !is_boot_cpu();
+    bool quiet = (chip_id == T8142 && !is_boot_cpu()) || s2r_quiet();
     if (!quiet) {
         if (!is_boot_cpu())
             uart_puts("RVBAR entry on secondary CPU");
